{
  "content": "<p><strong>Instructor:</strong> Dennis Freeman</p>\n<p><strong>Description:</strong> Three examples of Fourier transforms in action are given: removing noise from an electrocardiogram signal, using laser diffraction to calculate the groove spacing on CDs and DVDs, and determining the structure of DNA via x-ray crystallography.</p>\n",
